{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1298564-technocracy-versus-the-greek-gods-pjo","id":1298564,"title":"Technocracy versus the Greek Gods (PJO)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-22T05:25:36-07:00","id":1298564,"title":"Technocracy versus the Greek Gods (PJO)","content":"So me, and a friend of mine on Spacebattles, are currently trying to write a story involving a cross between mage the ascension and percy jackson. Several members of the technocracy cross over in a dimensional accident. And then, since they're mages, they can see through the Mist... and realise to their horror, that no one else can. The mortals of this world are chattel, looked over by superpowerful spirits. They can not see the things hunting them, let alone defend themselves. No one defends them. No one cares for them. <br /> <br /> And so these technocrats vow that they would do their duty, and drive away these dimensional aliens, and their hybrid progeny. They would build the technocracy anew, one man, one invention, one database at a time. They would keep the world safe, safe from everything that would harm them. They would make reality safe for the Masses. <br /> <br /> And so begins technocracy, PJO edition... <br /> <br /> Question. What would be interesting here? What would be good to see? What story ideas can there be? Mind you, its a story, not a role playing session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T05:37:32-07:00","id":1299564,"title":"","content":"So one thing to consider - possibly they CAN'T see through the Mists completely. Keep in mind that mages aren't immune to Changeling mists, and that is about the closest analog. But, perhaps they can catch glimpses, see parts. And then have to react to what they can see. Like hunters!<br /> Also, keep in mind that most of the demigods in PJO are teenagers. You may make some adjustments in your story if you wish, it is your world, but in the PHO world as it is, the kids are usually the ones fighting. So the technocrats will be fighting kids, and that will absolutely have implications if you go that route.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T20:24:09-07:00","id":1299829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EndlessKng</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1298564-technocracy-versus-the-greek-gods-pjo?p=1299564#post1299564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So one thing to consider - possibly they CAN'T see through the Mists completely. Keep in mind that mages aren't immune to Changeling mists, and that is about the closest analog. But, perhaps they can catch glimpses, see parts. And then have to react to what they can see. Like hunters!<br /> Also, keep in mind that most of the demigods in PJO are teenagers. You may make some adjustments in your story if you wish, it is your world, but in the PHO world as it is, the kids are usually the ones fighting. So the technocrats will be fighting kids, and that will absolutely have implications if you go that route.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm... true. <br /> <br /> I was thinking of their focus on fighting monsters, mad ghosts, and all the other nasties that exist, that our demigods stumble across. <br /> <br /> On the Mists.... I'm not sure. Can't they pierce it with their own tech? I mean, I'm fairly sure there's a void engineer/ Progenitor/ Iteration X Device that would let you pierce through illusions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T04:53:08-07:00","id":1299904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1298564-technocracy-versus-the-greek-gods-pjo?p=1299829#post1299829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm... true. <br /> <br /> I was thinking of their focus on fighting monsters, mad ghosts, and all the other nasties that exist, that our demigods stumble across. <br /> <br /> On the Mists.... I'm not sure. Can't they pierce it with their own tech? I mean, I'm fairly sure there's a void engineer/ Progenitor/ Iteration X Device that would let you pierce through illusions.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an interpretation thing. You cN play it that way if you want to, but I think that the mists in changeling (which again, seem to be eerily similar to their PJO counterparts) work on you harder proportionately to banality. And the other thing is they impact memory too. Even if the techno can pierce them, they would have a hard time remembering what they saw.<br /> I may be wrong though... dreaming isn't my strongest suit. And again, if you want to change it you could. But just mentioning what I recall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T05:21:03-07:00","id":1299911,"title":"","content":"Play?<br /> <br /> More like writing. <br /> <br /> I'm writing a story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T05:22:49-07:00","id":1299913,"title":"","content":"But thanks anyway","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T16:25:39-07:00","id":1301182,"title":"","content":"Hi.<br /> <br /> So... Technocracy. <br /> <br /> There are mostly 2 factions. <br /> <br /> 1. Take over the masses. They can't think for themselves. <br /> 2. Help the masses. They deserve our help. <br /> <br /> Question. <br /> <br /> If there's no consensus, no paradox, no weakening of reality barrier via consensus change.<br /> <br /> So... Would they allow demigods to join them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T05:59:28-07:00","id":1301593,"title":"","content":"It depends on the individual mages, but in general the Technocracy it's open to whomever would accept to follow the party line. Following the party line often implies things like accepting to be routinely brainwashed (albeit some radical Technocrats are against that) and being under permanent surveilance (privacy is not a right but a luxury to be earned under the Technocracy).<br /> <br /> So sure, demigods can get the job. But they're not demigods, that's an archaism, they're...umm...archetypically empowered humans or something like that. And having such strong ties with EDE's they have to be under constant monitoring to be usre they're not being used as pawns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T06:55:18-07:00","id":1301609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1298564-technocracy-versus-the-greek-gods-pjo?p=1301593#post1301593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends on the individual mages, but in general the Technocracy it's open to whomever would accept to follow the party line. Following the party line often implies things like accepting to be routinely brainwashed (albeit some radical Technocrats are against that) and being under permanent surveilance (privacy is not a right but a luxury to be earned under the Technocracy).<br /> <br /> So sure, demigods can get the job. But they're not demigods, that's an archaism, they're...umm...archetypically empowered humans or something like that. And having such strong ties with EDE's they have to be under constant monitoring to be usre they're not being used as pawns.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about if I restrict it to technocrats whose goal is 'help and protect and uplift the masses', instead of 'take over, control the Masses and crush all reality deviance'. <br /> <br /> Which brings me to another thing. <br /> <br /> Consensus. <br /> <br /> If the consensus doesn't really affect anything, except make it slightly harder for monsters to roam, and slightly empower the gods and give paradox, would the technocracy still continue the masquerade or crush Reality Deviants? I mean, I'm not too familiar with Mage The Ascension, but I'm fairly sure that the reasoning behind the technocracy's Progrom was that Reality Deviants were tearing apart the skeins of reality and letting in all the nasty spirits and stuff. So for the good of all, they had to kill them or convert them. <br /> <br /> Now that killing them won't solve the problems of the monsters, and Paradox only occurs because I don't want this to be a total stomp, so... what to do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T07:56:57-07:00","id":1301624,"title":"","content":"About the Consensus &quot;not affecting anything&quot;.<br /> <br /> 1\u00ba I see no way the Technocrats would know that. Mages do not have a Rote to know that the consensus exists and their metaphysics are right. Mages know that the Consensus exist trough experimentation, because belief makes their milacres easier to perform and easier to share with the masses, and because it makes harder or easier for monsters and hostile powers to roam. And most of that it's still true.<br /> <br /> Technocrats would only start to theorize that the Consensus isn't working here when they fail to update the Time Table (to improve the technology of the world) several times w/o significant monster interference, and even then it would be a crazy theory until something not related to their experimets advances technology in a dramatic enough way as to suspect that science doesn't need to be &quot;helped&quot; in this world.<br /> <br /> Even then the Consensus IT'S working insofar as it affects Paradox, which happens to be rather important for Mages<br /> <br /> 2\u00ba It matters not on their goal to crush Reality Deviants...other than they wouldn't be called with that name anymore. The primary objective of the Technocracy it's to kill the monsters that roam the night to empower humans as the masters of the world. Technocracy at it's most idealistic are human (sometimes trans-human) supremacists. They only care for &quot;the good of all&quot; insofar &quot;all&quot; includes humanity.<br /> <br /> All Technocracy factions assume that they have to help the masses<i> because they are helpless.</i> This it's what irked them and placed the Order of Reason against the monsters, wizards and other supernatural bullies in the first place.<br /> <br /> Thechnocrats are people and thus many have come to enjoy their control and power over the masses as an end instead of a mean, a lot of the leadership got corrupted. This caused the divide you're mentioning. But you're wrong in assuming that to take over the masses it's contradictory with helping them. Controling humanity it's a tool for that goal because, as put by the Men in Black : &quot;A <i>person </i>is smart. <i>People </i>are dumb, panicky, dangerous animals, and you know it!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Obviously the importance of controling the Paradigm and &quot;what people thinks&quot; would diminish if it isn't a proven way of killing the monsters (note that it may take centuries for the Technocrats to realize that), but that only means they cannot trust Reason and technology as a tool to eradicate the threaths. This could give the Pogrom a greater relevance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-01-2019, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T08:26:08-07:00","id":1301635,"title":"","content":"Wow. Your view of the technocracy is much higher than quite a few I've met. I'm quite Stephen lea sheppard himself said they were about control now. <br /> <br /> Irregardless, does this mean that:<br /> <br /> 1. I can lower paradox<br /> 2. I can have them join in with any faction, as long as they're friendly with humans? <br /> 3. Can I have more info on the technocracy's nicer side?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T08:28:52-07:00","id":1301638,"title":"","content":"By the way, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a>, since you think so well of the technocracy, what's your opinion on the traditions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T10:29:46-07:00","id":1301681,"title":"","content":"Oh, no, Technocracy it's all about control...but this isn't so selfish if you think that &quot;control&quot; means &quot;security&quot;. In our world we see lot's of times people resigning their freedom in the name of security. Airports control everything you have in your package, goverment places cameras in every street to prevent crime, the Alphabet organizations controls what you write in online forums just in case you're planning a terrorist attack...<br /> <br /> It's both fascinating and frightening that all of this CONTROL get's accepted in the name of security...and that people don't care about the fact that all of this (cameras in all places, spying) are methods that have been implemented <i>in</i> <i>prisions </i>before they got repackaged and marketed to the populace.<br /> <br /> I think that the debate between the Technocracy and the Traditions it's the classic debate between Security and Freedom.<br /> <br /> One wants to control what you do, what you want and what you think, because they know best (the proverbial overbearing parent)...The other would allow you to fly, leave you be, and if that means getting too close to the sun and burning, well, you brought that on yourself pal.<br /> <br /> Neither side it's &quot;right&quot;. Both have virtues and flaws, like most idealistic groups. <hr /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. I can lower paradox </div> </div> </div>Absolutely, Paradox it's dependant on the setting.<br /> <br /> First thing a Technocrat should do when entering an alternate universe should be to see what things cause Paradox (and unlike the truth of the universe, Paradox can be detected. Void Engineers have devices to detect if a procedure it's going to be Vulgar in the current environment)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. I can have them join in with any faction, as long as they're friendly with humans? </div> </div> </div>&quot;Friendly&quot; it's, perhaps, not enough to join in good faith.\u200b Theirs it's a &quot;my way or the highway&quot; + &quot;for the greater good&quot; mentality. Technocrats have a Plan, a Time Table, and don't like stuff that deviates from their vision of a better tomorrow.<br /> <br /> Also I imagine they would be pretty paranoid at the beginning. They come form the World of Darkness, a place where you trust nobody or die young.<br /> <br /> Technocrats may form temporary aliances with factions that are friendly to humans in order to fight against factions that are clearly a greater evil (has happened before, the Technocracy allied with the Traditions against the Nephandi in WW2), but they wouldn't trust them easily.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Can I have more info on the technocracy's nicer side? </div> </div> </div>Just read any of their Revised Convention books. However take what it's said with a grain of salt, after all these are technocrats talking about themselves (obviously they have a great opinion on themselves). The Guide of the Technocracy it's a bit outdated, but it's more honest about the good and the bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-01-2019, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T12:23:24-07:00","id":1301708,"title":"","content":"Note that, because in your setting there's few technocrats, what they believe as individuals it's more important than what the Technocracy believes. <br /> <br /> They could be opposed to brainwash. More or less tolerant of the supernatural. A combination of hardliners with others that have their own views...<br /> <br /> What the Technocracy believes may be better to have as background for these characters than the defining factor. You know, it's part of their story but even Technocrats are individuals and can make choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-01-2019, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T20:18:05-07:00","id":1301794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1298564-technocracy-versus-the-greek-gods-pjo?p=1301708#post1301708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that, because in your setting there's few technocrats, what they believe as individuals it's more important than what the Technocracy believes.<br /> <br /> They could be opposed to brainwash. More or less tolerant of the supernatural. A combination of hardliners with others that have their own views...<br /> <br /> What the Technocracy believes may be better to have as background for these characters than the defining factor. You know, it's part of their story but even Technocrats are individuals and can make choices.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Maybe I can make the void engineer extra hardliner, what with being forced to constantly fight off incursions by EDE and other assorted nasties, so he's viewing anyone who interacts with, or is one of them, with suspicion and lots of... hostility. <br /> <br /> While the syndicate and the NWO man don't really care, since, well, they aren't constantly being threatened with death by them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T20:41:49-07:00","id":1301798,"title":"","content":"Well, when you write the story please post a link to it. I'll check for it on Space Battles too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T20:56:20-07:00","id":1301803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1298564-technocracy-versus-the-greek-gods-pjo?p=1301681#post1301681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, no, Technocracy it's all about control...but this isn't so selfish if you think that &quot;control&quot; means &quot;security&quot;. In our world we see lot's of times people resigning their freedom in the name of security. Airports control everything you have in your package, goverment places cameras in every street to prevent crime, the Alphabet organizations controls what you write in online forums just in case you're planning a terrorist attack...<br /> <br /> It's both fascinating and frightening that all of this CONTROL get's accepted in the name of security...and that people don't care about the fact that all of this (cameras in all places, spying) are methods that have been implemented <i>in</i> <i>prisions </i>before they got repackaged and marketed to the populace.<br /> <br /> I think that the debate between the Technocracy and the Traditions it's the classic debate between Security and Freedom.<br /> <br /> One wants to control what you do, what you want and what you think, because they know best (the proverbial overbearing parent)...The other would allow you to fly, leave you be, and if that means getting too close to the sun and burning, well, you brought that on yourself pal.<br /> <br /> Neither side it's &quot;right&quot;. Both have virtues and flaws, like most idealistic groups. <hr /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. That's nice to hear. I'm usually on the technocracy side. But... well...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;Friendly&quot; it's, perhaps, not enough to join in good faith.\u200b Theirs it's a &quot;my way or the highway&quot; + &quot;for the greater good&quot; mentality. Technocrats have a Plan, a Time Table, and don't like stuff that deviates from their vision of a better tomorrow.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Also I imagine they would be pretty paranoid at the beginning. They come form the World of Darkness, a place where you trust nobody or die young.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Technocrats may form temporary aliances with factions that are friendly to humans in order to fight against factions that are clearly a greater evil (has happened before, the Technocracy allied with the Traditions against the Nephandi in WW2), but they wouldn't trust them easily.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that the various monsters and beasts would not endear them to the Percy Jackson world. <br /> <br /> By the way, does this mean that I can have them join in on the various battles? Like that fight in Manhattan? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Just read any of their Revised Convention books. However take what it's said with a grain of salt, after all these are technocrats talking about themselves (obviously they have a great opinion on themselves). The Guide of the Technocracy it's a bit outdated, but it's more honest about the good and the bad.</span><br /> <br /> </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>I was wondering about that. Does Revised weaken or nerf them in any way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T21:03:09-07:00","id":1301805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1298564-technocracy-versus-the-greek-gods-pjo?p=1301798#post1301798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, when you write the story please post a link to it. I'll check for it on Space Battles too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forums.spacebattles.com/threads/wi-technocracy-m-the-ascension-meets-pjoverse-and-the-greek-gods.736795/page-2#post-56127514\" target=\"_blank\">https://forums.spacebattles.com/thre...#post-56127514</a><br /> <br /> I made a short snippet, involving the recruitment of a demigod.<br /> <br /> And this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The debriefing:<br /> <br /> Audio transcript<br /> <br /> Date: [data expunged]<br /> <br /> [Log Begins]<br /> <br /> <br /> Interrogator: Carson, you are under here for debriefing. Please, tell us, what happened, as well as the details of the meeting with the three hybrids?<br /> <br /> Carson: Darn it, you suit. I told you not to call them hybrids. Anyway, here's what happened. Me and the boys, were there on some tip about some disruption. Sensors had picked up a trail of monster concentration. Must have been a dozen or so of them.<br /> <br /> Interrogator: please use the term, Carson. Its 'mutant pheromone detector'<br /> <br /> Carson: yeah yeah. I can't bear with the names you eggheads come up with. Any way, the detectors were going off crazy. Then we turned into an alleyway and found them.<br /> <br /> Interrogator: the children?<br /> <br /> Carson: yep. Fighting like the devil's of hell, they were. They were backed up against an alleyway. One tall kid. Boy, actually. Slumped to the ground, bleeding from the torso. Two girls, one 13 and another 11. Fighting the hell out of the dozen or so freaks trying to kill them. Kept their cool even through the threats.<br /> <br /> Interrogator: what threats?<br /> <br /> Carson: things like 'children of the gods, we will eat you!' or 'we will butcher you with knives made from your bones!' nasty stuff. Anyway, Larry must have heard enough, cause he gave the order to fire. And we all did. Those sweet guns you gave us made short work of those things. And then Nikara rushed over. Girls were so scared, they nearly stabbed her. Took her some time to cool them down and show we weren't monsters. Even stuck out her mouth to show it wasn't a snake. Then patched them up. Hehe he. <br /> <br /> Interrogator: and then?<br /> <br /> Carson: Well.. It was damned kids. They looked half starved. Scared. We gave them some of our rations, and they tried to warn us off. Real sweet of them. Tried telling us more people will try to kill them. We asked them if they meant the monsters. Then they fell real quiet. Then they started nodding. Guess they were shocked an adult could see them.<br /> <br /> Interrogator: the illusion. The phenomenon that prevents people from seeing the state of the world they are in.<br /> <br /> Carson: that it is.<br /> <br /> [At this point Carson lights a cigarette. This breach of etiquette is put on his file] <br /> <br /> interrogator: [coughs]. Put that out.<br /> <br /> Carson: you're no fun. [puts out lighter] anyway, Nikara finished patching them up. Those kids weren't going anywhere. Not with one injured and almost being killed. So Brad, bless him, offered to take them back.<br /> <br /> Interrogator: and you let him?<br /> <br /> Carson: duh. I mean, we're the good guys, aren't we? Shouldn't we be shooting monsters and saving kids? To bring science and enlightenment to a cruel world. Otherwise, what we're for?<br /> <br /> Interrogator: [sigh] fine. You can go now.<br /> <br /> Carson: just one question. What wee the names of those kids? We never got them.<br /> <br /> Interrogator: Thalia, Luke, and Annabeth. Please go. </div> </div> </div>Mind you, there won't be more. I just got banned. For a month.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T03:04:18-07:00","id":1301840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1298564-technocracy-versus-the-greek-gods-pjo?p=1301794#post1301794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. Maybe I can make the void engineer extra hardliner, what with being forced to constantly fight off incursions by EDE and other assorted nasties, so he's viewing anyone who interacts with, or is one of them, with suspicion and lots of... hostility.<br /> <br /> While the syndicate and the NWO man don't really care, since, well, they aren't constantly being threatened with death by them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Careful there. While, yes, the Void Engineer will be full of suspicion and mistrust at first, they are *also* the type to accept somebody being on their side when they have proven to fight a common enemy or indeed have shown to help each other out in a pinch. I.e. the VE's are very non-bullshit. You pull one of their asses out of the fire, they pull yours out of the flames, and you might make a good bud for life; Because on the frontier that's what counts and makes you survive.<br /> <br /> The NWO on the other hand? They never trust. They NEVER drop paranoia. The whole convention is about blackhats and mirrorshades, cloak &amp; dagger operations, mental conditioning, watching out for signs of 'deviancy', psychological control and manipulation. Even if they treat you as a temporary ally, they will never trust you, never have you leave their sights, don't trust the other conventions, and don't even trust each other for the most part.<br /> Mind you, they might not *show* it - but behind that calm demeanor, they always are breathing down your neck. The NWO is the Union's police and capital-A Agents - internally and externally. They *are* the Partyline.<br /> <br /> The Syndicate on the other hand, while I'd not say they 'trust', they are very good at understanding motivations. VERY good. Once the Syndicate knows what your spiel is, they are pretty secure in how they can turn the relationship into a 'give and take' one. They are the big masters of the Give And Take, after all. They even hire Traditionalists and other ilk at times for special missions, they have business relations with vamps, etc., so they actually might have more experience with handling deviant relations than even the VEs, which are second only to the Syndicate when it comes to that - though the VE's are at the top when it comes to honest relations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-02-2019, 06:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T08:49:14-07:00","id":1302231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1298564-technocracy-versus-the-greek-gods-pjo?p=1301803#post1301803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that the various monsters and beasts would not endear them to the Percy Jackson world.<br /> <br /> By the way, does this mean that I can have them join in on the various battles? Like that fight in Manhattan?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br /> <br /> Technocrats usually have sleeper agents and technomagical constructs doing their dirty work, but until they've got an infraestructure they will need to work with what they have. Without the Union to back them up I would expect a survival/frontier mentality to creep in. But they're mages, they will want to get involved in stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was wondering about that. Does Revised weaken or nerf them in any way? </div> </div> </div>Nope.<br /> <br /> Well, Revised does nerf ALL magick (in some ways, with Wonders and Rituals magick may be stronger), but that's just crunch stuff (dices and successes that aren't seen in fiction) and are optional in M20. In the fluff the only &quot;nerf&quot; they've got it's the Dimensional Anomaly (the Avatar Storm) killing most the high-ups, severing the Union from Control.<br /> <br /> One background choice would be if your agents are from before or after the Storm, but the historical stuff from the book it's useful regardless of that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, very well put.<br /> <br /> VE rarely are hardliners because against the horrors of the Umbra any help it's well recived, pointy hat or not. They're also more likely to enter actual fights (them and the It-X being the most militarized Conventions).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T19:05:01-07:00","id":1302416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1298564-technocracy-versus-the-greek-gods-pjo?p=1302231#post1302231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure.<br /> <br /> Technocrats usually have sleeper agents and technomagical constructs doing their dirty work, but until they've got an infraestructure they will need to work with what they have. Without the Union to back them up I would expect a survival/frontier mentality to creep in. But they're mages, they will want to get involved in stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Nope.<br /> <br /> Well, Revised does nerf ALL magick (in some ways, with Wonders and Rituals magick may be stronger), but that's just crunch stuff (dices and successes that aren't seen in fiction) and are optional in M20. In the fluff the only &amp;quot;nerf&amp;quot; they've got it's the Dimensional Anomaly (the Avatar Storm) killing most the high-ups, severing the Union from Control.<br /> <br /> One background choice would be if your agents are from before or after the Storm, but the historical stuff from the book it's useful regardless of that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Indeed, very well put.<br /> <br /> VE rarely are hardliners because against the horrors of the Umbra any help it's well recived, pointy hat or not. They're also more likely to enter actual fights (them and the It-X being the most militarized Conventions).</div> </div> </div> </div>So what do the technocracy do when fighting the Greek gods and the various enemies. <br /> <br /> I mean, the Greek gods say that they represent fundamental underpinnings of western civilization. Without them, the world goes poof. <br /> <br /> So is it way out there for the technocracy to make something like The Loom of Fate, a physics engine for reality itself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T07:16:09-07:00","id":1302543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1298564-technocracy-versus-the-greek-gods-pjo?p=1302416#post1302416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what do the technocracy do when fighting the Greek gods and the various enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>As stranded mages on a different world, it kinda depends on them. It wouldn't be out of character if some just want to go home, but having that barred I imagine they would try to establish a &quot;new Technocracy&quot;.<br /> <br /> A typical Syndicate would earn money and influence, trying to capitalize whatever this world knows as power to fund the project. A typical NWO would infiltrate the goverment, the army, or the police. It-X and Progenitors would start producing stuff and helping people. VE would try to understand how EDE's (Spirits) work in this world, analyze what threats are possible to face and what treaths are to be avoided. All would want to understand how the world ticks (for instance, how to get Quintessence here) and who or what are their enemies (and potential allies).<br /> <br /> After that they would probably try to go as normal, trying to undermine superstition, reinforce science and kill reality deviants (dangerous ones being more of a priority than good ones).<br /> <br /> A few changes are to be expected dependant on the characters (i.e. they could choose to neglect Room 101 if they aren't fans of brainwash. They could chose to be more or less hostile to the supernatural). Control isn't here the keep them in check, but it should be mentioned that they choosed to do this and why.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1298564-technocracy-versus-the-greek-gods-pjo?p=1302416#post1302416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, the Greek gods say that they represent fundamental underpinnings of western civilization. Without them, the world goes poof.<br /> <br /> So is it way out there for the technocracy to make something like The Loom of Fate, a physics engine for reality itself?[</div> </div> </div> </div>Short story: Yes, it is way out there. But let's analize why.<br /> <br /> Such a cosmic reality warping feat would fall, at least, under the highest ends of Magick. Let's try to *map* the kind of magick we're talking about, because the kind of absolute knowledge and infinite power such a feat would require goes way, WAY, beyond having all Spheres at 5. But, believe it or not, <u>similar</u> feats (though perhaps not *quite* as potent) were mentioned in Mage.<br /> <br /> *<u>Voormass final solution</u>:<br /> <br /> One of the ends of the world for Ascencion faces us against Archmaster Voormass plans to put an end to Death itself. By breaking the Wheel of Dharma and replacing it with *himself* he hopes to create an universe of absolute statism where nobody will die. Ever. Nobody would be able to live either in this new world because there will be no *change*, but he sees that as a slmall price.<br /> <br /> The book doesn't asume that Voormass can actually pull this out, it merely assumes that if he *casts* his spell Ascencion could become unreachable regardless if he fails or not. But being a little generous and assuming the crazy archmaster knew what he was doing, this is certainly an universal alteration.<br /> <br /> Now, I would think that to create an engine to sustain reality should be harder than Voormass plans to stop Death. Death it's only one aspect of Reality, you hope to replace all of them<br /> <br /> And Voormass, to have *hope* of achieving a lesser goal had Entropy 7, a unique relic chargued with the acumulated power of 1/4 of all Avatars of the world, had stolen the divinity of an aspect of the godess Kali, connected some of the most powerful corrupted Nodes of the world to suply Quintessence with the right Ressonance, and was casting the spell from the Shard Realm of Entropy itself (the Realm of the Umbra that represents and empowers the ArchSphere he was going to use)<br /> <br /> *<u>The fabled Archspheres</u><br /> <br /> \u200bMasters of the Art talks about Archspheres, Spheres above 5 and up to 10 (albeit they're described only to the 9 level). The 9th level of Archspheres usually has some power with cosmic implications, like the power of creating new laws of physics (Forces 9) or the power to create universes with Prime 9 (ontologically dependant on the universe where they are created). I would say that the power to stabilize a universe it's arround that level (8-10. 10, I think).<br /> <br /> But mages on that level (Oracles and Exemplars) are beyond the Ascencion War, and thus beyond Factions<br /> <br /> <u>Bottom Line</u><br /> <br /> These feats are things that would be difficult to achieve even for the collective might of the Technocracy. One of the reasons the Technocracy hopes to control the Consensus it's because they can't just tell the universe what to do (Reality!, I want no more dragons!). The Consensus it's the combined power of the Avatars of millons of humans, and thus manipulating it it's like a big ritual to warp reality.<br /> <br /> Now, if it's out there for the Technocracy itself, then it's way, WAY, out there for a group of technocrats stranded on another universe to try anything similar. They just wouldn't have the know-how nor the power. Unless, perhaps, the stranded mages were the Inner Circle of the Technocracy, <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <u>There's a chance?</u><br /> <br /> A posibility could open if one of the technocrats reaches Ascencion as the culmination of the character's arc. Anyone can Ascend, it isn't the realm of powerful archmages (it's actually harder for them to Ascend) , and there are legends of Ascended mages being able to affect all of Reality at once. A technocrat could create or become &quot;the Loom of Fate&quot; that way, but Ascension it's not a mcguffin to be tossed as a solution to a problem, it's a story. It *has* to be a heavy focus of the plot and the character to not sound <i>super forced</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-04-2019, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T07:49:54-07:00","id":1302550,"title":"","content":"^ That<br /> <br /> And if, by chance, the Archsphere system is *not* being used (It is...very...optional in M20) and the limit of the ultimate reach and ability of Level 5 Spheres is pretty much dependant on the amount of successes you gather up...then it becomes a matter of:<br /> <br /> 0) Step Zero. Figure out how the Technocrats even can think of how to do this, with their Paradigm(s)<br /> 1) A lot, *lot*, *LOT* of successes gathered over time and stored in...some manner<br /> 2) 'storing' those successes somewhere, somehow over time, which in itself might require another huge undertaking along the lines of building a sort of metaphysical cointainment of the accumulated magickal energy<br /> 3) Hoping nobody turns it off, on, sideways or upside-down in a way it isn't supposed to be, ever (Remember, Walter Pex was right..)<br /> 4) Hope no enemies the Technocrats ever find out about it<br /> 5) Hope that no literal deity Godhead is even remotely among those enemies<br /> 6) Possibly a lot of adventures, quests, perils and trials to find the mundane and metaphysical resources that aid, boost or even simply make this all possible<br /> 7) A couple decades worth of in-game time. Or longer.<br /> 8) Hoping that in the entire process you figure out a way to mitigating Botches to small amounts of work in the overall scheme - you don't want to handle this gargantuan task in any way, shape or form as a single 'Ritual'.<br /> 9) Fire ze charged up mystical/technocratical, supercharged, absolute-insanity-plan what-is-wrong-with-you McGuffin<br /> 10) ???<br /> 11) As you were, citizen<br /> <br /> ALTERNATE ENDING: gargantuan_explosion.mp3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-04-2019, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T08:50:21-07:00","id":1302572,"title":"","content":"Damn, that sounds hard. <br /> <br /> This story was meant to last at least a decade. <br /> <br /> Hmm..... <br /> <br /> Maybe I should just have it so that the gods were bullshitting about being the underpinnings of western civilization. Yeah, bullcrap they hitched themselves to, to make themselves look important or puff up their egoes or maybe its half truth. Maybe they aren't really avatars of western civilization.... they just bonded to it and used the portfolio to make themselves metaphysically bigger. But if you sever them from it....<br /> <br /> This takes some work. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T02:44:47-07:00","id":1302768,"title":"","content":"Quite frankly?<br /> I'd still make it all about the Consensus. Just *that* world's consensus - and only the Technocrats are even *aware* of it. Maybe even those Gods are oblivious to how it *works*.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> The Gods are so ingrained into general civilization of that world, that essentially the whole thing is a Reality Zone with those Gods and their 'rules' as the turning point.<br /> Which is not unlike how parts of the world were in the normal WoD's olde times, Dark Ages and before.<br /> <br /> So, the solution for the Technocrats? History repeating. Find the people who do *not* like living under those Gods. Find the people who are the easiest to sway towards the Technocrat's side.<br /> Build an &quot;Order Of Reason - Reloaded&quot;<br /> <br /> Essentially begin their task anew. Yes, it will take Generations and probably won't be anything the current characters will see from start to finish...but it would be helluva Roleplay. Gathering the people over time, doing so covertly to avoid detection, trying to subtly build up economic or political influence, meanwhile tinkering on inventions (Probably mostly made by the VE), and keeping an eye out on social shifts and also trying to get on the good side of supporters of those Gods - to know your enemy.<br /> Political Intrigues meet Powerbase Building meet Social Manipulation meet a subtle Arms Race and Army Gathering. And each character can play out their strength.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T05:12:45-07:00","id":1302785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1298564-technocracy-versus-the-greek-gods-pjo?p=1302768#post1302768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite frankly?<br /> I'd still make it all about the Consensus. Just *that* world's consensus - and only the Technocrats are even *aware* of it. Maybe even those Gods are oblivious to how it *works*.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> The Gods are so ingrained into general civilization of that world, that essentially the whole thing is a Reality Zone with those Gods and their 'rules' as the turning point.<br /> Which is not unlike how parts of the world were in the normal WoD's olde times, Dark Ages and before.<br /> <br /> So, the solution for the Technocrats? History repeating. Find the people who do *not* like living under those Gods. Find the people who are the easiest to sway towards the Technocrat's side.<br /> Build an &quot;Order Of Reason - Reloaded&quot;<br /> <br /> Essentially begin their task anew. Yes, it will take Generations and probably won't be anything the current characters will see from start to finish...but it would be helluva Roleplay. Gathering the people over time, doing so covertly to avoid detection, trying to subtly build up economic or political influence, meanwhile tinkering on inventions (Probably mostly made by the VE), and keeping an eye out on social shifts and also trying to get on the good side of supporters of those Gods - to know your enemy.<br /> Political Intrigues meet Powerbase Building meet Social Manipulation meet a subtle Arms Race and Army Gathering. And each character can play out their strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do know this is a fanfiction, right? <br /> <br /> That means that we probably can't leave characters behind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T05:43:09-07:00","id":1302800,"title":"","content":"Having that in mind, remember that characters often have long term goals that aren't fully realized in the story (even when the story hasn't an open ending). Now, for good or ill, we know what was the future of the Rebelion in Star Wars and what happened to Luke, but back when the original movies made legend we didn't know that. There's nothing wrong for characters to have a future.<br /> <br /> All that matters it's what kind of story you want to tell. One thing it's to tell the story of the overthrowing of the gods in 10 years, and another to tell the story of the foundation of the Technocracy in another world. In the second case the <i>posibility</i> of defeating the gods can be tossed as part of an open ending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T05:52:07-07:00","id":1302802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1298564-technocracy-versus-the-greek-gods-pjo?p=1302785#post1302785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do know this is a fanfiction, right?<br /> <br /> That means that we probably can't leave characters behind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, the things that fanfiction can do...<br /> <br /> Seriously, in the realm of fanfiction don't feel like you're forced to be limited in any way to 'those characters need to stay'. A lot of good fanfiction goes, as Aleph said, at some point past the original source material - and possibly even the original characters, doing what-ifs and maybes of people that come after - especially previous main character's progeny or the progeny of frieds and related people.<br /> <br /> Though I understand if you want to stick to the well-knowns, of course. But yes, that limits the timeframe...and the open ending option that Aleph mentioned might be the way to end the story. Show struggles and victories, hardships and big successes in that decade timeframe, but then hint at the end of bigger things to come. Because in that short timeframe, the whole of reality (or global consensus) just can't be turned inside out.<br /> <br /> Of course ultimately you also have the creative freedom to..bend the rules a bit <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Pun intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T06:11:34-07:00","id":1302806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1298564-technocracy-versus-the-greek-gods-pjo?p=1302800#post1302800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having that in mind, remember that characters often have long term goals that aren't fully realized in the story (even when the story hasn't an open ending). Now, for good or ill, we know what was the future of the Rebelion in Star Wars and what happened to Luke, but back when the original movies made legend we didn't know that. There's nothing wrong for characters to have a future.<br /> <br /> All that matters it's what kind of story you want to tell. One thing it's to tell the story of the overthrowing of the gods in 10 years, and another to tell the story of the foundation of the Technocracy in another world. In the second case the <i>posibility</i> of defeating the gods can be tossed as part of an open ending.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno. Maybe start 10 years before canon? Start recruiting before hand? <br /> <br /> I mean, I started out with them recruiting Luke, Annabeth, and Thalia. <br /> <br /> You seem to know this stuff better than me. Two questions: <br /> <br /> 1. These are cream of the crop, Arete 5, top of their convention dudes. They know that magic exists. They know what they're doing is magic. What can they do in 10 years? At least, in comparism to the greek gods?<br /> 2. I've seen in the Dark age and Progenitor convention book that the technocracy has access to anti aging treatments. How good are they, and how do they interact with the modern world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T06:15:20-07:00","id":1302808,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, can I link this thread to SB? <br /> <br /> I'm writing this with space penguin and inawariminister.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T07:57:49-07:00","id":1302824,"title":"","content":"Sure, I'd have no problem with that!<br /> Hello to all, if you're reading this<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1298564-technocracy-versus-the-greek-gods-pjo?p=1302806#post1302806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. I've seen in the Dark age and Progenitor convention book that the technocracy has access to anti aging treatments. How good are they, and how do they interact with the modern world?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, technically one of the leaders of the NWO is an ex-member of the Cult Of Ecstasy, who fought against Nephandi in WW2. And he's still lookin' good. Page 63, NWO Revised.<br /> By the way, he was born in 1732.<br /> <br /> So yeah, both Mystics and Technocrats pretty much have the same 'rules' for it all - they can go on for hundreds or even thousands of years in some famous cases if justified, necessary or when wanting to in the first place - some paradigms and personal opinions kind of escew exceeding your natural life for no reason. The problem for both factions is that, by the rules, reality starts to slowly pile up Permanent Paradox if you exceet your natural lifespan.<br /> <br /> It's less of a game balance thing, and more a fluff thing that explained in earlier editions (before the Avatar Storm) , why there weren't boatloads of Mages aged hundreds of years running around on Earth. The reason it's mostly fluff also explains why the Unaging merit is so cheap.<br /> <br /> The only way to avoid that Permanent Paradox is to stick to Sanctums, Constructs, the Umbra or other realms where living very long and prosper is just no issue. Essentially the supernaturally older you are as a Mage, the more you are forced to stay away from Earth if you want to perform Magick.<br /> <br /> Sooo...in the case of a world shaped by Greek Gods? Could go either way, really.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-05-2019, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T08:12:38-07:00","id":1302829,"title":"","content":"Hmm... Daedalus lasted for, like, Millenia. <br /> <br /> Then again, he was cursed. And in a sanctum of sorts. <br /> <br /> Hmm.... <br /> <br /> I guess that they can use progenitor memory drugs and anti aging drugs as a hook. People have dreamt immortality for a long time. And now its within reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T08:26:19-07:00","id":1302833,"title":"","content":"Yas.<br /> There are other famous millenia-old-mage examples, like Medea (Marauder Oracle - and yes, it's *the* Medea. Jason and the Argonauts. Arete 10, too. ), Al-Aswad (The 'first' nephandus) or Lilith ( Whom some groups of Verbena see as their first. ).<br /> There are some quite ancient Mages out there indeed, but by that age they are probably as alien as your average godhead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-05-2019, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T08:32:39-07:00","id":1302836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. These are cream of the crop, Arete 5, top of their convention dudes. They know that magic exists. They know what they're doing is magic. What can they do in 10 years? At least, in comparism to the greek gods?</div> </div> </div> </div>In comparison to the greek gods I can't tell because right now I'm not versant on PJO lore. I can help you on the Mage side of things.<br /> <br /> Your characters are, basically, capable of reaching Mastery (if barely). That doesn't say a lot about them but I would guess they're potent Adepts or weak Masters, Sphere wise. And Rank wise between <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ranks_and_Titles_in_Mage:_The_Ascension\" target=\"_blank\">Experts and Masters</a> . They are above average, true, but probably less powerful than Arete 7 <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Augustine_Aleph\" target=\"_blank\">General Aleph</a> (who is, in turn, <i>below </i><a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Control\" target=\"_blank\">Control and the Inner Circle</a>). Is this right for you?<br /> <br /> If that's the case, well, as <i>Ambrosia </i>said the limits of Spheres at 5 aren't very clear, and they probably can reach that power in 10 years if they don't have it already. What they *can* do would depend more on their training and on the Spheres that they have than Arete or Rank. And even knowing that it would be easier to say what they *won't* be able to do<br /> <br /> What would <i>you </i>want them to be able to do?<br /> <br /> One interesting thing it's that at these levels magick starts becoming less dependant on the Mage itself. By creating Wonders or altering the properties of Life and Matter you can give supernatural powers to other people so they go and fight for you, with Correspondence you can help others from afar, and with Time you can &quot;hold&quot; effects in places or people to trigger when you need them.<br /> <br /> To give you a (super Vulgar but, I hope, <i>clear</i>) example:<br /> A high level Progenitor could &quot;inspire&quot; herself on the greek gods work and create a retrovirus that temporarily transforms a person into a man-bull giant with just a word on the cellphone (uses a ritual that takes the form of carefuly preparing the virus in a lab to cast a Time 4/Life 5 hanging a transmutation effect. When the &quot;code word&quot; it's said trough a phone the subject transforms into a classic monster).<br /> Add Mind 4 to have complete control of the monster, Mind 3 should be enough if you just want to send it into a blind rage.<br /> With Prime 5 instead of Time 4 you could give someone the power to transform into a minotaur at will (but this is Vulgar and would accumulate Paradox each time the power it's used...to be discharged on the poor sod, not the mage). Arguably Life 5 it's enough to give someone the power to transform at will, but then it's a permanent mutation and risks Pattern Bleeding (suffering damage each day)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. I've seen in the Dark age and Progenitor convention book that the technocracy has access to anti aging treatments. How good are they, and how do they interact with the modern world? </div> </div> </div>They're very good altrough they become harder the older you are. And they react to the modern world by gathering Permanent Paradox if you live beyond 150 years. This Paradox can be avoided if you live off-world (or in a Sanctum), but it will kick in the moment you get to Earth. Most ancient mages either live off-world or in a Sacntum<br /> <br /> Nowadays anti-aging it's the poor-man's choice of immortality. Instead, making a clone and transfering your mind/avatar to it when you get old or die it's all the rage among puissant Masters. If your technocrats had the luck of having a Progenitor with the know how (Life 5 to craft the body, Mind 5 to move &quot;the software&quot;. And high levels of Science, obviously), they could do this, which may have the boon of allowing a mage to have a &quot;backup &quot;in case he gets killed (you would need Mind 5, Correspondence 5, Time 4 to do that)...But it's entirely possible for even a &quot;cream of the top&quot; Progenitor to not have the know-how to do all of that (it's very potent magick). Note that this method accrues Permanent Paradox with time, too.<br /> <br /> <i>Looking </i>younger it's easier than living beyond your years (it's just Life 2-3, and with nowadays beauty surgery it's probably Coincidental)<br /> <br /> And, as <i>Ambrosia </i>hinted, in a parallel universe (a world ruled by greek gods) you can change how Paradox works to some extent. Certain things can be easier or harder to pull off","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-05-2019, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T22:06:49-07:00","id":1303007,"title":"","content":"I am aware of the insanity that high level mages are capable of, thank you very much. <br /> <br /> Urm... if I wish to have characters which are powerful, won't die when facing down a greek god, and also able to interact with normal humans, how powerful should I make them? More than Arete 5? <br /> <br /> Actually, I think I may have made them too weak. Go to Arete 7!<br /> <br /> *begins thinking hard* <br /> <br /> I want them to not die. I want them to thrive. Percy's a high end demigod. He's described, not accurately, as a living hurricane or storm, paired with supreme sword skills and invincibility. Gods, monsters, demons... I want them to fade in the background, as a hurricane. <br /> <br /> Basically, the greeks and romans got gods on their side. I want the technocrats to not roll over and die from them. <br /> <br /> Additionally, a question. I've already written up a snippet of them shooting up a bunch of monsters. <br /> <br /> What would they tell their new recruits? <br /> <br /> 1. Hey, this is super science we're doing. We're a secret organization dedicated to taking down the monsters and making mankind the masters of the universe<br /> 2. Hey, this is actually magic, dressed up as science. We're a group of technomages seeking to transform mankind into gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T00:28:46-07:00","id":1303024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1298564-technocracy-versus-the-greek-gods-pjo?p=1303007#post1303007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would they tell their new recruits?<br /> <br /> 1. Hey, this is super science we're doing. We're a secret organization dedicated to taking down the monsters and making mankind the masters of the universe<br /> 2. Hey, this is actually magic, dressed up as science. We're a group of technomages seeking to transform mankind into gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they'd focus on their of those things immediately. The Order Of Reason's original statements went along the lines of wanting to make the world a *safer* place for mankind. Pulling them away from the things that go bump in the night, empowering them to travel without fear of not making it out of the woods, allowing their children to grow up without being whisked away by weird spirits, etc.<br /> <br /> It was a very..noble approach, and less a blunt 'We are the masters of the everything'. They applied to the people who *were* afraid of the things out there, or oppressed by mad mages, etc.<br /> I think that approach to new recruits would work best. The rest, including the introduction to the methods and arms of the Enlightened comes later - and if the Technocrats just busted the new recruits from the claws of some monstrosity, their strange gadgetry's first impression also is &quot;Wow, this just saved my life!&quot; or &quot;I was supposed to be unhealable, this is amazing!&quot;<br /> <br /> I.e. positive first impressions and promises to get people out of Bad Things. Heroes, not Conequerors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-06-2019, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T00:37:39-07:00","id":1303026,"title":"","content":"As this thread came from SB, I'll post the same thing here as I did there.<br /> It all boils down to whether the Technocracy have any weapons that can harm Kaiju sized gods that could actually arm wrestle Cthulhu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1762-rogerd","name":"RogerD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T00:53:47-07:00","id":1303031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RogerD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1298564-technocracy-versus-the-greek-gods-pjo?p=1303026#post1303026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As this thread came from SB, I'll post the same thing here as I did there.<br /> It all boils down to whether the Technocracy have any weapons that can harm Kaiju sized gods that could actually arm wrestle Cthulhu.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are mages. <br /> <br /> Worse, mages from Mage: The ascension. <br /> <br /> They'll manage, one way or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T15:03:46-07:00","id":1303413,"title":"","content":"Ok. Here's another thing: <br /> <br /> Primium countermagic. Or more accurately, demigod countermagick. Should I allow the technocrats to throw bad luck and coincidental effects at them willy-nilly? Or should I let them nullify a certain level of magic before they start getting hurt. I say this because I just remembered a procedure/ spell, that let the technocrat inflict large amounts of horrible luck on a person. For an hour. <br /> <br /> 1. Should demigods get countermagick?<br /> 2. Should demigods get to Awaken and get their own magic?<br /> 3. Is there even greek magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T07:09:47-07:00","id":1303524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RogerD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1298564-technocracy-versus-the-greek-gods-pjo?p=1303026#post1303026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It all boils down to whether the Technocracy have any weapons that can harm Kaiju sized gods that could actually arm wrestle Cthulhu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't know a lot about those gods but mages are infamous for their nukes. Albeit they don't use them very often 'cause they're hard to make and Paradoxical.<br /> <br /> One of the Tradition most potent weapons (the orb that sits at the center of Horizon Realm) can completely obliterate supernatural foes of the size of a mountain range (that's way bigger than most kaijus), and Forces 6 Porthos was supposed to be able to summon sligthly lower levels destruction all by himself. The wars in the Umbras has seen kaijus deployed and killed, and the Technocracy can make nukes to kill spiritual beings and concepts.<br /> <br /> In other words, dealing with beings of the size of a kaiju isn't any problem for powerful mages, just like overpowering Cthulhu strenght isn't really a hard thing to do (he was left unconcious by ramming him with a large boat). It's their <i>mystical potency</i> what could make beating them a hard sell. Cthulhu isn't fearsome because he's big or strong, he's fearsome because he's an alien god with the power to remake the world<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Should demigods get countermagick?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they resist supernatural influence regularly, I would assume so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Should demigods get to Awaken and get their own magic? </div> </div> </div>Well, that opens an interesting question: Awakening it's possible only to those that have a sleeping Avatar. Since mages aren't natural of this universe I would argue that there shouldn't be any Avatar in this world other than those brought by the mages. Thus the only way for mages to be born in this world would be a mage dying and the avatar reincarnating in a baby (that assuming the Avatars would reincarnate in this universe). Such a charcter could become a mage, and if the Avatar is one of those who share it's Past Lives, could even have some knowledge about WoD and the Technocracy<br /> <br /> If then that baby it's a demigod...things get interesting. A very easy assumption to make would be that since WoD isn't kind with hibrid splats (no vampi-mage, no were-mage) then such a combo wouldn't be doable. However those that know their Merits and Defects would know that Nephilims are the sons and daugthers of the spirits of the high umbra, some of whom are godlike conceptual beings like, say, the High Umbral version of the Greek Gods. And they can totally Awaken, perhaps even easier than normal humans.<br /> <br /> BUT <u>should</u> they?.<br /> <br /> There's an argument against it, for narrative reasons: Such a &quot;chosen one&quot; can be seen as an &quot;authors pet&quot; or even &quot;mary sue&quot;-ish <i>due to rarity alone</i>, especially by those WoD fans that don't know Nephilim are a thing in Mage (it was a very obscure rule until the recent release of BoS). From the perspective of WoD readers, it may hold a strong Samuel Haight(tm) vive and thus predispose some against it.<br /> <br /> On the other hand I'm not sure if PJO fans wouldn't find it interesting to have a character with growing powers of a different nature (that offers a chance to explain how they work from the rock bottom with a PJ character perspective), and Sammy does have it's fans too.<br /> <br /> It's a risk you should ponder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Is there even greek magic? </div> </div> </div>Of course there's greek magic. Do you mean in real life, Mage, or PJ world?<br /> <br /> <u>Real life</u>:<br /> People believed in magic back then. They had augurs and oracles, witches and priests including secret mystery orders like the Orphics and the Pythagoreans with lots of esoteric secrets. There's a TON of gods, to the point each family has a god for their own. Talismans were commonplace. Far away lands like egypt hold secrets that the Greeks sometimes admired as magical too.<br /> <br /> <u>Mage</u>:<br /> There were loads of mage groups there. From the top of my mind you have:<ul><li>The Hippocratic Circle, ancestors of the the Progenitors.</li> <li><a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Pythagoras_(WOD)\" target=\"_blank\">Pythagoras </a>himself was a great mage and one of the antecesors of what would become the Order of Hermes (perhaps even THE founder of their Paradigm). His disciples divided into two factions, the Acusmatics and the Mathematics that warred among themselves and would end becoming ther ancestors of the OoH and the Technocracy.</li> <li>The Hierochtonoi, worshipers of the chthonic gods were Underworld focused wizards that latter would form part of the Euthanatos</li> <li>The Dionysian cults and several divination practices were the ancestors of the Seers of Chronos/Cult of Extasy</li> <li>In the foudation of the Order of Reason, Daedalus is taken as an example of how mages should work (albeit if Dedalus was an early technomancer or just a legend it's unknown)</li> <li>The Orphic Circle had mages among it's ranks. The legendary Orpheus it's the inspiration of a lot of Underworld related magick</li> <li>And, of course anywhere there's nature gods, sacrifices and witches, the ancestors of the Verbena have to be close.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-08-2019, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T08:52:59-07:00","id":1303536,"title":"","content":"PJ world. <br /> <br /> Also, another thing. I think we should put it as 'everyone has an avatar' only for certain metaphysical reasons, the presence of gods crushed them into sleep... until the technocracy came. <br /> <br /> Now they can awaken. I mean seriously? Only 5 people with Avatars? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T22:11:52-07:00","id":1304105,"title":"","content":"Frack it. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> ? Can we talk about this on questionable questing? The format here makes my eyes bleed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link"